## Quick Verdict
The function is **working**, but it’s a single monolith that mixes *API plumbing*, *text‑analysis*, and *logging* all in one.  
Refactoring it into a few focused modules will:

| Goal | Why it matters |
|------|----------------|
| **Separation of concerns** | Easier to test, maintain, and replace parts (e.g., swap BLEU‑ROUGE library). |
| **Eliminate magic numbers** | Constants + config keep thresholds in one place and make the scoring logic readable. |
| **Make the scoring rules extensible** | New rules can be added without touching the core loop. |
| **Improve type safety & documentation** | TS types & JSDoc keep the API clear. |
| **Reduce duplicated regex work** | Compile regex once, reuse them, and avoid repeated `match()` calls. |
| **Structured logging** | Capture all relevant metrics in a single object rather than scattered log messages. |

Below is a high‑level refactor plan with concrete code snippets.  
Apply the changes incrementally (unit‑test after each step) to keep the module functional.

