## 1️⃣  Centralise the “bench‑function” mapping

Instead of a `switch` you can keep a map from `BenchmarkType` → evaluation function.  
This removes a lot of duplicated `try / catch / logger` boilerplate and makes it trivial to add a new benchmark.

```ts
// benchmarks/benchmarkMap.ts
import type { BenchmarkType } from 'shared/types/aiQualityBenchmark.js';
import { evaluateJSONAssembly } from './evaluateJSONAssembly.js';
import { evaluateCreativeWriting } from './evaluateCreativeWriting.js';
import { evaluateTaskPlanning } from './evaluateTaskPlanning.js';
import { evaluateTypescriptQuality } from './evaluateTypescriptQuality.js';

export const benchmarkFunctions: Record<
  BenchmarkType,
  (modelId: string, serverId: string) => Promise<number>
> = {
  'json-assembly': evaluateJSONAssembly,
  'creative-writing': evaluateCreativeWriting,
  'task-planning': evaluateTaskPlanning,
  'typescript-quality': evaluateTypescriptQuality,
};
```

---

## 2️⃣  Extract helper factories for results

Both success and failure cases follow the same shape, so a tiny factory hides the repetition.

```ts
// benchmarks/benchmarkResult.ts
import type { BenchmarkType, QualityBenchmarkScore } from 'shared/types/aiQualityBenchmark.js';

export function makeResult(
  type: BenchmarkType,
  score: number,
  rubric: string,
  timestamp = new Date().toISOString()
): QualityBenchmarkScore {
  return { type, score, rubric, timestamp };
}

export function makeFailureResult(
  type: BenchmarkType,
  err: unknown
): QualityBenchmarkScore {
  const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);
  return makeResult(
    type,
    0,
    `Failed: ${message}`,
    new Date().toISOString()
  );
}
```

---

## 3️⃣  Run benchmarks in parallel (optional)

Benchmarks are independent, so they can be executed concurrently.  
Using `Promise.allSettled` lets us collect the results without aborting the whole run on a single failure.

```ts
// benchmarks/runQualityBenchmarks.ts
import { logger } from 'shared/logging/logger.js';
import type { BenchmarkType, QualityBenchmarkScore } from 'shared/types/aiQualityBenchmark.js';
import { benchmarkFunctions } from './benchmarkMap.js';
import { makeResult, makeFailureResult } from './benchmarkResult.js';

/**
 * Runs quality benchmarks for a given model and server combination.
 *
 * @param modelId – The model identifier to benchmark
 * @param serverId – The server identifier hosting the model
 * @param types – Array of benchmark types to run
 * @returns Promise resolving to a map of benchmark results
 */
export async function runQualityBenchmarks(
  modelId: string,
  serverId: string,
  types: readonly BenchmarkType[]
): Promise<Record<BenchmarkType, QualityBenchmarkScore>> {
  logger.info(`[Benchmark] Running quality benchmarks for model ${modelId} on server ${serverId}`);

  const tasks = types.map(async (type) => {
    const evalFn = benchmarkFunctions[type];
    const rubric = `Automated ${type} evaluation`;

    try {
      logger.debug(`Running benchmark: ${type}`);
      const score = await evalFn(modelId, serverId);
      logger.info(`Benchmark ${type} completed with score: ${score}`);
      return [type, makeResult(type, score, rubric)] as const;
    } catch (err) {
      logger.error(`Error during quality benchmark for type ${type}: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`);
      return [type, makeFailureResult(type, err)] as const;
    }
  });

  const settled = await Promise.allSettled(tasks);

  // Build the final Record
  const results: Record<BenchmarkType, QualityBenchmarkScore> = {} as any;
  settled.forEach((s) => {
    if (s.status === 'fulfilled') {
      const [type, score] = s.value;
      results[type] = score;
    }
  });

  return results;
}
```

### Why this is better

| What changed | Why it matters |
|--------------|----------------|
| `switch` → `benchmarkFunctions` map | Adds a single source of truth for which function runs which benchmark. Adding a new benchmark is a one‑liner. |
| Result factories | Eliminates copy‑pasted boilerplate, guarantees consistent shape, and keeps all formatting logic in one place. |
| `Promise.allSettled` | Runs benchmarks concurrently, reducing wall‑time, while still collecting every result (including failures). |
| Stronger typing (`Record<BenchmarkType, QualityBenchmarkScore>`) | Keeps the compiler happy; no unsafe casts. |
| Logging in one place | All log messages are generated inside the helper, making it easier to adjust formatting or add tags later. |

---

