## Quick Take‑away

The snippet is already very small and clear, but a few tiny changes can make it even more maintainable, testable and type‑safe:

| What to change | Why it matters | How to do it |
|----------------|----------------|--------------|
| **Define a dedicated interface for the input payload** | Gives you a single place to document the expected structure, allows IDEs and the compiler to catch typos, and keeps the function signature tidy. | ```ts<br>export interface AggregatedAIModelNodePayload {<br>  modelId: string;<br>  aggregatedMetrics: Record<string, unknown>;<br>  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;<br>}<br>``` |
| **Destructure the payload in the function signature** | Keeps the body short, removes repetitive `modelData.` prefixes, and lets the compiler infer the types automatically. | ```ts<br>export async function createAggregatedAIModelNode({<br>  modelId,<br>  aggregatedMetrics,<br>  metadata,<br>}: AggregatedAIModelNodePayload): Promise<Node> { … }``` |
| **Introduce a constant for the node type** | Avoids magic strings; if you ever need to rename or reuse the type, you only edit one spot. | ```ts<br>const NODE_TYPE = 'ai-model' as const;<br>``` |
| **Merge the metadata in one clear step** | Avoids the risk of accidentally mutating either source and makes the intent obvious. | ```ts<br>const mergedMetadata = {<br>  ...aggregatedMetrics,<br>  ...metadata,<br>};<br>``` |
| **Add a more detailed JSDoc block** | Good for documentation generators and for other developers to know *why* you’re creating an aggregated node. | ```ts<br>/**<br> * Persists an aggregated AI‑model node.  The node’s title is derived from the `modelId` and its metadata is a shallow merge of the supplied `aggregatedMetrics` and `metadata` objects.<br> *<br> * @param payload - The payload needed to create the node.<br> * @returns The newly created {@link Node}.<br> */``` |
| **Keep the return statement simple** | `return node;` is fine, but you can also return the awaited promise directly: `return ensureNode({ … });`. This removes the intermediate variable and reduces a line of code. | ```ts<br>return ensureNode({<br>  type: NODE_TYPE,<br>  title: `Aggregated Metrics for ${modelId}`,<br>  metadata: mergedMetadata,<br>});<br>``` |
| **Optional – add error handling** | If `ensureNode` can throw, you might want to surface a more domain‑specific error or log the failure.  This is especially useful in larger services. | ```ts<br>try {<br>  return await ensureNode({ … });<br>} catch (err) {<br>  // eslint-disable-next-line no-console<br>  console.error('Failed to create aggregated AI model node', err);<br>  throw err;<br>}<br>``` |
| **Consider exporting the interface** | If other modules need to validate the same shape, they can import `AggregatedAIModelNodePayload`. | ```ts<br>export { AggregatedAIModelNodePayload };``` |

---

## Refactored Code

```ts
import { ensureNode } from 'shared/node/nodeService.js';
import { Node } from 'shared/types/index.js';

/**
 * Payload for creating an aggregated AI‑model node.
 */
export interface AggregatedAIModelNodePayload {
  /** The identifier of the AI model. */
  modelId: string;

  /** Metrics that have been aggregated for this model. */
  aggregatedMetrics: Record<string, unknown>;

  /** Any additional metadata that should be stored on the node. */
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;
}

const NODE_TYPE = 'ai-model' as const;

/**
 * Persists an aggregated AI‑model node.
 *
 * The node’s title is derived from the `modelId` and its metadata is a shallow merge
 * of the supplied `aggregatedMetrics` and `metadata` objects.
 *
 * @param payload - The payload needed to create the node.
 * @returns The newly created {@link Node}.
 */
export async function createAggregatedAIModelNode({
  modelId,
  aggregatedMetrics,
  metadata,
}: AggregatedAIModelNodePayload): Promise<Node> {
  const mergedMetadata = { ...aggregatedMetrics, ...metadata };

  return ensureNode({
    type: NODE_TYPE,
    title: `Aggregated Metrics for ${modelId}`,
    metadata: mergedMetadata,
  });
}
```

### Why this version is better

| Area | Improvement |
|------|-------------|
| **Readability** | Destructuring removes repetitive prefixes; a single `mergedMetadata` variable makes the merge obvious. |
| **Maintainability** | A named constant (`NODE_TYPE`) and a shared interface keep all related details in one place. |
| **Type‑safety** | The payload interface forces callers to provide all required properties, and the compiler can warn if you miss a field or pass the wrong type. |
| **Extensibility** | If you ever need to change the node type or add more fields, you modify just the interface or the constant. |
| **Documentation** | The JSDoc block now explains *what* the function does, *why* you use the payload shape, and what the caller can expect. |

---

## Bottom Line

