summary:
**What’s happening**

The file contains dozens of **duplicate method definitions**.  
Only one of each function is needed – the rest will never be called and
break TypeScript because a class cannot declare the same method twice.

**Where the duplicates sit**

| Duplicate pair | What it does |
|----------------|--------------|
| `buildPerformanceRelations` / `buildServerlessRelations` | Build the performance & serverless node & its relations |
| `buildPerformanceNode` / `buildServerlessNode` | Create/merge the performance & serverless nodes |
| `registerPerformanceRelation` / `registerServerlessRelation` | Make sure a relation exists, create if needed |
| `updatePerformanceRelation` / `updateServerlessRelation` | Update an existing relation |
| `registerNodeWithRelation` | Helper that creates a relation if it does not exist |
| `findParentNodeForChild` | Find a parent node from a list |
| `buildNodeRelations` | Orchestrate all of the above |
| `getNodeRelations` | Retrieve all potential parent nodes |
| `buildPerformanceRelations`, `buildServerlessRelations` | Called from `buildNodeWithRelations` (they need the `performanceNode` / `serverlessNode` that `buildNodeWithRelations` just created) |
| `updateNodeMetadata` | Merge the original node with performance & serverless info |

Everything else in the file is a copy‑paste of those 8–10 logical
operations.

---

### Refactor plan

1. **Keep a single instance of each helper** – delete the repeated blocks.
2. **Group related helpers** in the same section of the class.
3. **Rename the helpers to make the intent clear** (e.g. `ensureRelation`,
   `updateRelation`, `createRelationIfMissing`).
4. **Move shared logic (e.g. fetching by title) into one private method**.
5. **Unit‑test the new class** – the old duplicates may have subtle side‑effects
   that must be preserved.

